Spec: Authorized private route provider boundary

Purpose:
  Allow the trusted Agent to obtain dynamic transport endpoints without exposing routing or runtime management to applications.

Owns:
  ./ConnectionRoutes.cs

References:
  ./LocalAccess.sdd

Must:
  Mint immutable route scopes only from current caller-bound local access; include all identity and grant generations in the pool key.
  Keep provider endpoints and lifecycle private to trusted Agent composition, never part of control RPC or application SDK.
  Pass the original absolute monotonic deadline and per-waiter cancellation to acquisition; route release must not stop unrelated leases.
  Invalidate owned routes on network generation changes and allow authority/currentness checks without accepting self-declared caller data.
